you all can go to dinner together or  it's hard when you don't all have the  same Saturday morning plans I get that  you were gonna have to be hyper  intentional Heather you're gonna have to  have to have to focus number two it may  be the kind of work you're doing these  are twelve hour shifts so I'm gonna  guess  you are a nurse in an ER you are a  firewoman or you're a surgeon and you're  working 12-hour shifts where you're  operating on brains or maybe you're  working on an oil rig out in the Gulf I  don't know but if you're working 12-hour  shifts at a job that's high high stress  with high high consequences then you've  got to be hyper intentional about taking  care of yourself taking care of your  community taking care of your  relationships all the stuff I just said  the last thing I want you to look at  Heather is this do you get nervous or  anxious before other things in your life  do you get anxious or nervous before  church before a date before your parents  come home to town or is it just about  work because if you get anxious or  nervous about other things when you  watch the news does your heart start  racing or if you see something about  climate change do you get that drop in  your stomach right or when you have to  stop and get gas in the car whatever it  may be I want you to step back from  focusing just on work I want you to look  around your entire ecosystem take a look  at your at your kitchen and see are  other places on fire because if it's  just about your job then that's an  answer in and of itself but if you're  struggling with anxiety in other places  you know you've got to do some deeper  heart work on Heather because it's not  the jobs fault it may be the  accountabilities fault it may be the  ecosystems fault it may be some deep  stuff you've got to deal with but you're  asking the right questions and there is  light at the end of this thank you so  much for your email Heather and while  we're here let's get one more email in  hey dr. 